    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI made the `householdId` deterministic from `(lastName, postcode)` and reworked the household/duplicate handling to key off it. Changes were kept small and confined to simple functions:\n\n1. **`HouseholdId.java`** (tiny class): `of(lastName, postcode)` now hashes `normalize(lastName) + \"|\" + postcode`, so owners with the same last name and postcode get the same 12-hex-char id automatically. (Only the input source changed \u2014 the SHA-256/hex formatting is untouched.)\n\n2. **`Owner.getHouseholdId()`**: one-line change to feed `postcode` instead of `address`. Since MapStruct maps this straight to `OwnerDto.householdId`, the API output is now the deterministic value.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1`**:\n   - `sameHousehold(a, b)` now compares the computed `getHouseholdId()` (last name + postcode) instead of last name + address. This is reused by the household-size (`householdMemberCount`) computation, so that input keys off the computed id.\n   - Added a household-duplicate block: if any existing owner shares the household id, return **409** unless the request sets `sharesHousehold`, which bypasses the block and creates the owner as a declared member.\n   - A created owner is no longer flagged as a possible duplicate (`possibleDuplicate=false`, `possibleDuplicateOf=null`) \u2014 a declared member is not a suspected duplicate, and any non-declared same-household create is now rejected before that point. Removed the now-unused `PossibleDuplicate` import.\n\nBehavior verified: same last name + postcode \u2192 same `householdId` (with `sharesHousehold` needed for the second create); different last name, same postcode \u2192 different `householdId`. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nStructural impact stayed low \u2014 four small edits across three files, each in a low-complexity function, with the `HouseholdId` hashing body and the `getIdentityKey`/`MembershipLevel` code left untouched.",
